README.md:293:## Terraform
README.md-294-
README.md:295:There are 3 available ways to deploy AHA, all are done via the same Terraform template to make deployment as easy as possible.
README.md-296-
README.md:297:**NOTE: ** AHA code is tested with Terraform version v1.0.9, please make sure to have minimum terraform verson of v1.0.9 installed.
README.md-298-
README.md-299-The 3 deployment methods for AHA are:
README.md-300-
README.md:301:1. [**AHA for users NOT using AWS Organizations using Terraform**](#aha-without-aws-organizations-using-terraform): Users NOT using AWS Organizations.
README.md:302:2. [**AHA for users WITH AWS Organizations using Terraform (Management Account)**](#aha-with-aws-organizations-on-management-or-delegated-administrator-account-using-terraform): Users who ARE using AWS Organizations and deploying in the top-level management account.
README.md:303:3. [**AHA for users WITH AWS Organizations using Terraform (Member Account)**](#aha-with-aws-organizations-on-member-account-using-terraform): Users who ARE using AWS Organizations and deploying in a member account in the organization to assume a role in the top-level management account.
README.md-304-
README.md:305:## AHA Without AWS Organizations using Terraform
README.md-306-
README.md-307-### Prerequisites
README.md-308-
README.md-309-1. Have at least 1 [endpoint](#configuring-an-endpoint) configured (you can have multiple)
README.md:310:2. Have access to deploy Terraform Templates with the following resources: AWS IAM policies, Amazon DynamoDB Tables, AWS Lambda, Amazon EventBridge and AWS Secrets Manager.
README.md-311-
README.md:312:**NOTE: ** For Multi region deployment, DynamoDB table will be created with PAY_PER_REQUEST billing mode insted of PROVISIONED due to limitation with terraform.
README.md-313-
README.md:314:### Deployment - Terraform
README.md-315-
README.md-316-1. Clone the AHA package that from this repository. If you're not familiar with the process, [here](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-clone) is some documentation. The URL to clone is in the upper right-hand corner labeled `Clone uri`
README.md-317-```
README.md:318:$ git clone https://github.com/aws-samples/aws-health-aware.git
README.md:319:$ cd aws-health-aware/terraform/Terraform_DEPLOY_AHA
README.md-320-```
README.md:321:2. Update parameters file **terraform.tfvars** as below
README.md-322- - *aha_primary_region* - change to region where you want to deploy AHA solution
README.md-323- - *aha_secondary_region* - Required if needed to deploy in AHA solution in multiple regions, change to another region (Secondary) where you want to deploy AHA solution, Otherwise leave to default empty value.
README.md:324: - *AWSOrganizationsEnabled* - Leave it to default which is `No`. If you do have AWS Organizations enabled and you want to aggregate across all your accounts, you should be following the steps for [AHA for users who ARE using AWS Organizations (Management Account)](#aha-with-aws-organizations-on-management-or-delegated-administrator-account-using-terraform)] or [AHA for users WITH AWS Organizations (Member Account)](#aha-with-aws-organizations-on-member-account-using-terraform)
README.md:325: - *AWSHealthEventType* - select whether you want to receive *all* event types or *only* issues.
README.md-326- - *Communications Channels* section - enter the URLs, Emails and/or ARN of the endpoints you configured previously.
README.md-327- - *Email Setup* section - enter the From and To Email addresses as well as the Email subject. If you aren't configuring email, just leave it as is.
--
README.md-331- - *ExcludeAccountIDs* - type ***just*** the name of the .csv file you want to upload if needed to exclude accounts from monitoring, else leave it to empty.
README.md-332- - *ManagementAccountRoleArn*  - In ARN of the AWS Organizations Management Account assume role leave it set to default None as this is only for customers using AWS Organizations.
README.md:333:3. Deploy the solution using terraform commands below.
README.md-334-```
README.md:335:$ terraform init
README.md:336:$ terraform plan
README.md:337:$ terraform apply
README.md-338-```
README.md-339-
